## Problem: The `public` access modifier is not allowed for static classes
The `public` access modifier cannot be used on static classes.

```java
public class NonStaticClass {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("This is non-static method");
    }
}
```

## Solution:
To fix the issue, you can declare the `static` variables as instance variables instead of global variables. Here's an example:

```java
public class NonStaticClass {
    private int result;

    public void setResult(int result) {
        this.result = result;
    }

    public static int getResult() {
        return this.result;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        NonStaticClass instance = new NonStaticClass();
        instance.setResult(10);
        System.out.println("The final result is " + NonStaticClass.getResult());
    }
}
```

